 integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $h(x)={x}^{3}-2$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =(-x)^{3}-2 \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-2 \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}+2) \\\\  & \\ne -h(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $f(x)={x}^{5}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{5}+(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{5}-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-({x}^{5}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{5}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{{x}^{2}})$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{(-x)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & \\ne -g(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534494 true] [17592186291877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291878 13194139534494 true] [17592186291877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291879 13194139534494 true] [17592186291877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291880 13194139534494 true] [17592186291877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291881 13194139534494 true] [17592186291877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291882 13194139534494 true] [17592186291877 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534494 true] [17592186291877 1041 "selection" 13194139534494 true] [17592186291877 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291882 13194139534494 true] [17592186291877 1110 #uuid "f459767b-797d-5350-848a-cf0ecc8e9d00" 13194139534494 true] [17592186291878 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534494 true] [17592186291878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534494 true] [17592186291878 1111 #uuid "e05cf006-4e35-5836-9c93-3b8d7516c161" 13194139534494 true] [17592186291879 1034 "I only" 13194139534494 true] [17592186291879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534494 true] [17592186291879 1111 #uuid "bf2aa493-2f19-5559-b2b5-b6fc6d11ec3f" 13194139534494 true] [17592186291880 1034 "III only" 13194139534